1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,536
I get paid to clean crime scenes before the bodies even hit the floor. My employer sends coordinates, I scrub the blood.

2
00:00:07,836 --> 00:00:17,940
It sounds impossible, but the system is relentless. Every detail must match the work order perfectly down to the final smudge.

3
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:25,848
Tonight, a new assignment pops onto my tablet. I open the file, and my heart drops into my hollow stomach.

4
00:00:26,148 --> 00:00:33,228
The coordinates point directly to apartment 4B. That is my apartment. My safe space. My home.

5
00:00:33,528 --> 00:00:40,776
I race through the rain, terrified I will find my sister shattered on the floor. I burst through the front door.

6
00:00:41,076 --> 00:00:49,284
The apartment is completely empty except for a stranger wearing the exact same silver suit as me, holding a bucket.

7
00:00:49,584 --> 00:00:57,456
He isn't scrubbing blood away. He is carefully spreading dark red paint onto the beige rug in precise streaks.

8
00:00:57,756 --> 00:01:06,132
I drop my bleach bottle. He turns slowly, pointing at the work order. 'We don't clean past crimes, kid. We plant them.'

9
00:01:06,432 --> 00:01:14,592
The mind sees blood and creates a killer. Every scene I ever prepped was a subconscious prompt for a future victim.

10
00:01:14,892 --> 00:01:21,372
Now I stare at the painted stain on my rug, feeling the urge grow. Who will clean up after me?
